# C style

`snake_case` for types, functions, files, and fields. Game translation units are C.

```c
/* good */
typedef struct arena_slice {
    uint8_t *data;
    size_t size;
} arena_slice;

void world_init(void);
```

```c
/* bad */
typedef struct WorldSlice { uint8_t *Data; } WorldSlice;
void WorldInit(void);
```

SoA is parallel arrays, not an array of structs that grows with `malloc`.

C++ is limited to `host/engine_host.cpp` and `host/st7789_drawer.cpp`. Those files may subclass PixelRoot32 types. They still use `snake_case` for new names.
